From: Tiberiu Chibici <chibicitiberiu@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 00:13:02 +0200
Subject: Game controllers: a DualShock plays with no setting (SDL game
 controller API)

Walnut is a console: the pad should drive the tank as it comes, while
BZFlag opens no joystick until one is picked under Options > Input, and
binds none of its buttons.

- joystickname defaults to "auto": the first SDL game controller, else
  the first joystick, else none without an error message.
- A game controller (a DualShock 3 is "PS3 Controller") is opened through
  SDL's game controller API, so its buttons and left stick are read by
  their place on the pad, whatever numbers the driver gives them:
  getJoyButtons() returns them in BzfJoystick::GameControllerButton order
  (the triggers count as pressed past half way), getJoy() the left stick,
  and the D-pad is in the buttons, not a hat. A plain joystick is read as
  before.
- Default bindings for those places (N = place + 1): Cross and R2 fire,
  Square and L2 jump, Circle drops the flag, Triangle identifies and
  starts (as I does: identify on press, restart on release), L1 the
  binoculars, Select the score. The left stick drives (the input switches
  to the joystick when it moves, as before).
- Where the buttons become key events (playing.cxx), on a game controller
  Start is Escape (the menu), the D-pad the arrow keys, and while a menu is
  up Cross is Return and Circle Escape. A release goes out as the event its
  press did. The "Press ... to start" line names the button Triangle
  (and no joystick button without a game controller).

The keyboard and mouse are unchanged; a saved configuration keeps its own
joystick and bindings.

Forwarded: not-needed

